title: Your first marker tiddler
type: text/vnd.tiddlywiki

A marker tiddler is one tiddler that defines one syntax mapping: a literal trigger (`open`) plus what to do when it fires (an HTML element, a TW widget call, a wrapping list container, ...). Every marker in the plugin is a tiddler tagged <<tag "$:/tags/CustomMarkup/Marker">> plus its vocabulary tag (the vocab tiddler's title, e.g. `vocab/markdown`).

!! Required fields

* `kind`. One of `glyph`, `glyph-level`, `word`, `inline-pair`, `list-item`. See [[Marker Kinds]] for what each one does.
* `open`. The literal text that fires the marker.
* `tags`. `$:/tags/CustomMarkup/Marker` plus the vocab tag (the vocab tiddler's title, e.g. `vocab/markdown`).

Optional fields cover the output (element, classes, attributes), parsing (mode, end-string, body-raw), editor integration (marker-icon, caption), and security (allow-unsafe). The full list lives in [[Marker Fields]].

!! Walkthrough: a `NOTE` keyword

Create a tiddler:

```
title: vocab/myvocab/NOTE
tags: $:/tags/CustomMarkup/Marker [[vocab/myvocab]]
caption: Note
kind: word
open: NOTE
mode: block
element: div
classes: .my-note
```

In any tiddler that activates `vocab/myvocab`, the line

```
NOTE Read the docs first.
```

renders as

```
<div class="my-note">Read the docs first.</div>
```

You also need a vocab meta tiddler titled `vocab/myvocab` tagged `$:/tags/CustomMarkup/Vocabulary` (the title itself is what each marker carries in its `tags`). See [[Vocabulary Meta Fields]] for the meta schema and [[Activate a vocabulary]] for how readers turn the vocab on.

